  <issue>
  qt.environ setting
Sometimes it can be useful to set environment variables for qutebrowser only. This can be done in `config.py` already, but having a setting would make things a bit easier (also to test via `--temp-basedir -s`.

In the config, this would be of `type: Dict` with `keytype: String` and `valtype: String`, as well as `restart: true` set (perhaps also `none_ok: true` so that `None` can be used as a value to remove a previously set variable).

Then qutebrowser would apply those in `qutebrowser/config/qtargs.py` or so, similar to how other settings (e.g. `config.val.qt.force_platform`) are already mapped to environment variables
  </issue>
  
